      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Enhanced border security and surveillance technology are essential first steps to stop illegal crossings, but they alone cannot solve the root causes of migration or integrate newcomers into the economy. Expanding pathways to citizenship and humanitarian processing is the only sustainable long-term solution because it provides legal certainty, boosts the workforce, and reduces the strain on social services by preventing the growth of undocumented populations. A bipartisan approach that prioritizes legal immigration over enforcement is the only way to ensure both economic growth and social stability.",
